Appendix G: Offline–Online Gap (Theorem 7)

Theorem 7. Let P^* be the true belief transition kernel under exact contact dynamics, and \widehat P the kernel induced by the complementarity‑free MPC scheme used online, with total‑variation error \|P^*(\cdot \mid b,c,a) - \widehat P(\cdot \mid b,c,a)\|_{\mathrm{TV}} \le \delta_{\mathrm{cf}} for all (b,c,a). Assume the optimal value function V^* is L_V-Lipschitz with respect to the state distribution in total variation. Then the value functions satisfy

|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}| \;\le\; \frac{\gamma L_V}{1-\gamma}\, \delta_{\mathrm{cf}}.

Proof.
The two value functions are the fixed points of the Bellman operators \mathcal{T}^* and \widehat{\mathcal{T}} with kernels P^* and \widehat P respectively:

V^{\text{offline}} = \max_{c,a} \bigl( r + \gamma P^* V^{\text{offline}} \bigr), \qquad
V^{\text{online}} = \max_{c,a} \bigl( r + \gamma \widehat P V^{\text{online}} \bigr).

Taking the supremum norm difference,

\begin{aligned}
\|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty 
&\le \gamma \max_{c,a} \bigl\| P^* V^{\text{offline}} - \widehat P V^{\text{online}} \bigr\|_\infty \\
&\le \gamma \bigl( \|P^* V^{\text{offline}} - P^* V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty + \|P^* V^{\text{online}} - \widehat P V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty \bigr) \\
&\le \gamma \|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty + \gamma L_V \delta_{\mathrm{cf}} .
\end{aligned}

Here we used that P^* is a contraction (in sup norm) and that for any belief b,

|(P^* V^{\text{online}})(b) - (\widehat P V^{\text{online}})(b)| \le L_V \,\|P^*(\cdot\mid b) - \widehat P(\cdot\mid b)\|_{\mathrm{TV}} \le L_V \delta_{\mathrm{cf}}.

Solving for \|V^{\text{offline}} - V^{\text{online}}\|_\infty gives the bound. ∎

